wrestle|sport|VERB|Grapple with an opponent|To grapple with another person, trying to hold or throw them, especially in a sport.|đấu vật; vật nhau|The athletes wrestled on the mat.|Các vận động viên đấu vật trên thảm.|Wrestle with someone; sport context.|-
well|adverb|ADVERB|In a good way|In a good, effective, or satisfactory way.|tốt; giỏi|She plays the piano well.|Cô ấy chơi đàn piano giỏi.|Adverb modifying verb; better, best.|0
well|healthy|ADJECTIVE|In good health|Healthy or feeling free from illness.|khỏe; khỏe mạnh|He is feeling well again.|Anh ấy lại cảm thấy khỏe.|Usually predicative.|1
well|interjection|INTERJECTION|Introduce a response|Used to introduce a response, pause, or change in the conversation.|à; được rồi|Well, let's discuss the next question.|Được rồi, chúng ta hãy bàn câu hỏi tiếp theo.|Discourse interjection; punctuation separates it.|2
well|water|NOUN|Water-access hole|A deep hole dug or drilled to reach water underground.|giếng|The village draws water from a well.|Làng lấy nước từ một giếng.|Countable.|3
young|adjective|ADJECTIVE|Early in life|Not having lived or existed for a long time.|trẻ; non|The young tree needs support.|Cây non cần được chống đỡ.|Young person or organism.|0
young|people|NOUN|Young people collectively|People at an early stage of life, considered as a group.|người trẻ|The programme encourages the young to read.|Chương trình khuyến khích người trẻ đọc sách.|The young; plural collective use.|1
young|offspring|NOUN|Animal offspring|The babies or immature offspring of animals.|con non|The bird protects its young.|Chim bảo vệ các con non của mình.|Plural collective young; no youngs.|2
witch|magic|NOUN|Woman associated with magic|A woman believed or portrayed to have magical powers.|phù thủy|The witch in the story lived in a forest.|Phù thủy trong truyện sống trong rừng.|Countable; fictional or belief context.|-
whereabouts|location|NOUN|Location|The place where someone or something is.|nơi ở; vị trí|Her whereabouts remained unknown.|Nơi cô ấy ở vẫn chưa được biết.|Often someone's whereabouts; singular or plural agreement occurs.|-
